  "_comment": "Full curriculum pool that poses every task kind currently wired through pkg/curriculum + rlenvadapter, so every rlenv action can become legal during training (when its preconditions are met). Built from configs/curriculum.json plus the newer action-space fields (equip/useitem, pickup, place, fly, ride, combat, creeper/spear/mace, follow, sleep/portal/light-portal, arrive_sneaking). Cross-cutting radii (sleep/portal/light_portal) are injected onto every episode; task kinds are selected uniformly among those with non-empty pools. Notes: (1) follow_target_player_names needs a second real connected player/bot already in the session; (2) portal/light_portal have no DefaultEpisodeSeeder yet \u2014 the working-area template must already provide a portal/frame within radius, or those actions stay masked as nothing-visible; (3) arrive_sneaking only affects goto dispatch. Sample values mirror production curriculum.json distances/radii and rlenv.DefaultConfig where a default already exists. task_weights boosts newer action-space kinds so the full pool does not dilute them to ~1/N each.",
